  "comments": [
    {
      "path": "lib/ui/features/settings/views/model_settings_view.dart",
      "content": "`widget.dataControls` is accessed three separate times here: pattern-matched twice inside the `localSections` collection-if (lines 139 and 151) and then extracted once more into `final dataControls` below (line 157). Consider hoisting the extraction to the top of `_body` alongside `themeSettings`/`languageSettings` (e.g., `final dataControls = widget.dataControls;`) and reusing that local in the collection-if. This removes the duplicated pattern matches, avoids the mildly confusing situation where two shadowed `dataControls` locals exist inside the list literal while a third is declared right after it, and keeps the null-check style consistent with how the other optional settings are handled.",
      "suggestion_code": "      if (dataControls != null)\n        ListenableBuilder(\n          listenable: dataControls,\n          builder: (context, _) =\u003e\n              _StoragePrivacySection(viewModel: dataControls),\n        ),",
      "existing_code": "      if (widget.dataControls case final dataControls?)\n        ListenableBuilder(\n          listenable: dataControls,\n          builder: (context, _) =\u003e\n              _StoragePrivacySection(viewModel: dataControls),\n        ),",
      "start_line": 139,
      "end_line": 144,
      "thinking": "Confirmed. I'll go ahead and post a comment about maintainability.",
      "category": "maintainability",
      "severity": "low"
    },
    {
      "path": "test/ui/features/settings/views/model_settings_view_test.dart",
      "content": "The rollback tests verify the UI state (mode restored, row key back to the committed value, alert shown) but never assert that nothing was persisted. Today that invariant is implicit because the fakes throw before assigning `savedMode`, but if a future fake (or a real repository being mirrored here) persists first and then reports failure, these tests would still pass. Consider keeping a reference to the fake (e.g. `final preferences = _FakeLanguagePreferences(failSave: true);`) and adding `expect(preferences.savedMode, isNull);` after the failed tap — same for the theme rollback test — to pin down the \"failed save leaves the repository untouched\" contract.",
      "existing_code": "    final languageViewModel = LanguageSettingsViewModel(\n      preferences: _FakeLanguagePreferences(failSave: true),\n      languageMode: languageMode,\n    );",
      "start_line": 90,
      "end_line": 93,
